Description: X11 demands-attention requests make the window urgent, as in i3
 Java, Wine and Qt programs ask for attention with a _NET_WM_STATE client
 message adding, removing or toggling _NET_WM_STATE_DEMANDS_ATTENTION. i3
 treats it like the ICCCM urgency hint; sway ignored it, while wlroots still
 added the atom to the window's _NET_WM_STATE. The request now drives the
 window's urgency under the urgency-hint rules (never for the focused window,
 urgent deny, force_display_urgency_hint), and the atom is kept in step with
 the urgency sway shows, whatever set or cleared it. A window that maps with
 the urgency hint or the atom already set is urgent once mapped, unless it
 takes the focus or a rule denies it.
 .
 for_window rules are checked again when a window becomes urgent, as i3 does,
 so rules with urgent= criteria can fire (each rule still runs once per
 window). urgent deny now also covers activation requests that would make the
 window urgent (swaywm/sway#9041). A window that unmaps while urgent no longer
 comes back urgent, and a window removing its WM_HINTS property no longer
 crashes sway.
 .
 The five upstream commits, squashed; they apply to 1.11 plus the series
 unchanged apart from context.
